From 560a7b540fbe0e5e7e9374bd768c78544be2311b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jhuan Reategui Solis <reateguisolisjm@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:06:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: retry DefaultAdapter on NoSuchAdapter while
 bluetoothd starts

bluetoothd registers on D-Bus before hci0 shows up; the event loop gave
up on the first org.bluez.Error.NoSuchAdapter and shut the whole stack
down. Retry every 10 ms instead.

(The NAP UUID workaround that used to live here is gone: NetworkServer
was missing because the Y210 kernel had CONFIG_BT_BNEP off, now fixed
in the kernel.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I95d9b6361f2fb6e249fd72c929682bdb732520f5
---
 core/jni/android_server_BluetoothEventLoop.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/jni/android_server_BluetoothEventLoop.cpp b/core/jni/android_server_BluetoothEventLoop.cpp
index 192e1e36d13..b8d2ac3616a 100644
--- a/core/jni/android_server_BluetoothEventLoop.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/android_server_BluetoothEventLoop.cpp
@@ -344,6 +344,12 @@ const char * get_adapter_path(DBusConnection *conn) {
                     LOG_AND_FREE_DBUS_ERROR(&err);
                     usleep(10000);  // 10 ms
                     continue;
+                } else if (dbus_error_has_name(&err,
+                    "org.bluez.Error.NoSuchAdapter")) {
+                    // bluetoothd up but hci0 not yet registered, retry
+                    LOG_AND_FREE_DBUS_ERROR(&err);
+                    usleep(10000);  // 10 ms
+                    continue;
                 } else {
                     // Some other error we weren't expecting
                     LOG_AND_FREE_DBUS_ERROR(&err);
-- 
